From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baocheng Su <baocheng.su@siemens.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:24:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] spi: cadence-qspi: Avoid DMA for non-DMA controllers

The Cadence QSPI AHB read path attempted dma_memcpy() for large reads
even when the controller was not configured for DMA. This can return
corrupted data when reading SPI NOR through the AHB window and cause
environment CRC failures on TI AM654 OSPI.

Only use the DMA copy path when is_dma is set, and fall back to
memcpy_fromio() for non-DMA controllers.

Signed-off-by: Baocheng Su <baocheng.su@siemens.com>
---
 drivers/spi/cadence_qspi_apb.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/cadence_qspi_apb.c b/drivers/spi/cadence_qspi_apb.c
index 0d4bc685f5db..c4c36e4ef456 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/cadence_qspi_apb.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/cadence_qspi_apb.c
@@ -774,7 +774,7 @@ int cadence_qspi_apb_read_execute(struct cadence_spi_priv *priv,
 	cadence_qspi_apb_enable_linear_mode(true);
 
 	if (priv->use_dac_mode && (from + len < priv->ahbsize)) {
-		if (len < 256 ||
+		if (len < 256 || !priv->is_dma ||
 		    dma_memcpy(buf, priv->ahbbase + from, len) < 0) {
 			memcpy_fromio(buf, priv->ahbbase + from, len);
 		}
